  "solution": "The logic followed here is,\n\nLogic: **Second Number = First Number × (Third Number ÷ 2)**\n\n**(14, 98, 14)**\n\n→ 98 = 14 × (14 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 98 = 14 × 7\n\n**(16, 144, 18) **\n\n→ 144 = 16 × (18 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 144 = 16 × 9\n\nNow, let's check each option,\n\n**1) (31, 198, 16) **\n\n→ 198 = 31 × (16 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 198 ≠ 31 × 8\n\n**2) (29, 122, 19)**\n\n→ 122 = 29 × (19 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 122 ≠ 29 × 9.5\n\n**3) (24, 187, 14) **\n\n→ 187 = 24 × (14 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 187 ≠ 24 × 7\n\n**4) (22, 132, 12)**\n\n→ 132 = 22 × (12 ÷ 2)\n\n→ 132 = 22 × 6 ⇒ **Satisfies the logic.**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"****(22, 132, 12)\"**.",
